window.POC_BANK=[{"id":"poc-001","concept":"Assessment","stem":"A new client reports chest pressure when climbing stairs but has never discussed it with a physician. What is the dental hygienist's BEST next step before beginning elective care?","choices":["Proceed but shorten the appointment","Complete treatment and document the symptom afterward","Clarify the symptom, assess urgency, and obtain appropriate medical consultation before elective care","Ask the client to sign a waiver"],"answer":2,"why":"Unexplained exertional chest pressure may indicate unstable cardiovascular disease. Assessment findings that could alter safety must be investigated before elective care.","zh":"不明原因的活动后胸部压迫感可能提示心血管疾病。开始选择性治疗前，应进一步评估并取得适当医疗咨询。","pearl":"New symptoms that may affect safety belong in assessment before treatment, not in documentation after treatment.","rationales":[{"en":"“Proceed but shorten the appointment” is not the best response. It moves ahead before the safety concern or current need has been assessed. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Unexplained exertional chest pressure may indicate unstable cardiovascular disease. Assessment findings that could alter safety must be investigated before elective care.","zh":"“Proceed but shorten the appointment”不是最佳处理。该做法在尚未评估安全问题或当前需要之前就继续治疗。 正确处理原则是：不明原因的活动后胸部压迫感可能提示心血管疾病。开始选择性治疗前，应进一步评估并取得适当医疗咨询。"},{"en":"“Complete treatment and document the symptom afterward” is not the best response. It moves ahead before the safety concern or current need has been assessed. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Unexplained exertional chest pressure may indicate unstable cardiovascular disease. Assessment findings that could alter safety must be investigated before elective care.","zh":"“Complete treatment and document the symptom afterward”不是最佳处理。该做法在尚未评估安全问题或当前需要之前就继续治疗。 正确处理原则是：不明原因的活动后胸部压迫感可能提示心血管疾病。开始选择性治疗前，应进一步评估并取得适当医疗咨询。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Ask the client to sign a waiver” is not the best response. A signature cannot replace assessment, disclosure, understanding, or valid consent. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Unexplained exertional chest pressure may indicate unstable cardiovascular disease. Assessment findings that could alter safety must be investigated before elective care.","zh":"“Ask the client to sign a waiver”不是最佳处理。签字不能取代评估、信息披露、理解和有效同意。 正确处理原则是：不明原因的活动后胸部压迫感可能提示心血管疾病。开始选择性治疗前，应进一步评估并取得适当医疗咨询。"}]},{"id":"poc-002","concept":"Assessment","stem":"Which item is part of the subjective assessment?","choices":["Blood pressure reading","Client's description of sensitivity when drinking cold water","Probing depth of 6 mm","Radiographic bone loss"],"answer":1,"why":"Subjective data come from what the client reports. Measurements and observed findings are objective data.","zh":"主观资料来自患者的描述；测量值和临床观察属于客观资料。","pearl":"Subjective = reported. Objective = observed or measured.","rationales":[{"en":"“Blood pressure reading” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Subjective data come from what the client reports. Measurements and observed findings are objective data.","zh":"“Blood pressure reading”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：主观资料来自患者的描述；测量值和临床观察属于客观资料。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Probing depth of 6 mm” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Subjective data come from what the client reports. Measurements and observed findings are objective data.","zh":"“Probing depth of 6 mm”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：主观资料来自患者的描述；测量值和临床观察属于客观资料。"},{"en":"“Radiographic bone loss” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Subjective data come from what the client reports. Measurements and observed findings are objective data.","zh":"“Radiographic bone loss”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：主观资料来自患者的描述；测量值和临床观察属于客观资料。"}]},{"id":"poc-003","concept":"Assessment","stem":"A client states that their medical history has not changed. What should the dental hygienist do?","choices":["Accept the statement without review","Review and update the history at every appointment and document the response","Repeat the entire written questionnaire only once every five years","Ask only about medications"],"answer":1,"why":"Medical history must be reviewed and updated regularly because changes can alter treatment decisions and risk.","zh":"每次就诊都应复核并更新病史，因为变化可能影响治疗决策和风险。","pearl":"“No change” is still an assessment finding and should be documented.","rationales":[{"en":"“Accept the statement without review” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Medical history must be reviewed and updated regularly because changes can alter treatment decisions and risk.","zh":"“Accept the statement without review”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：每次就诊都应复核并更新病史，因为变化可能影响治疗决策和风险。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Repeat the entire written questionnaire only once every five years” is not the best response. It is too narrow and omits other information required for safe, client-centred care. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Medical history must be reviewed and updated regularly because changes can alter treatment decisions and risk.","zh":"“Repeat the entire written questionnaire only once every five years”不是最佳处理。该做法过于片面，遗漏了安全且以患者为中心的护理所需信息。 正确处理原则是：每次就诊都应复核并更新病史，因为变化可能影响治疗决策和风险。"},{"en":"“Ask only about medications” is not the best response. It is too narrow and omits other information required for safe, client-centred care. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Medical history must be reviewed and updated regularly because changes can alter treatment decisions and risk.","zh":"“Ask only about medications”不是最佳处理。该做法过于片面，遗漏了安全且以患者为中心的护理所需信息。 正确处理原则是：每次就诊都应复核并更新病史，因为变化可能影响治疗决策和风险。"}]},{"id":"poc-004","concept":"Vital Signs","stem":"A client's blood pressure is substantially higher than their usual readings. What is the BEST first action?","choices":["Ignore the value because the client feels well","Repeat the measurement after proper positioning and a short rest","Begin instrumentation immediately","Diagnose hypertension"],"answer":1,"why":"An unexpected reading should first be verified using correct technique. Dental hygienists assess and refer; they do not diagnose hypertension.","zh":"异常读数应先用正确方法复测。牙科卫生师负责评估和转诊，而不是诊断高血压。","pearl":"Verify an abnormal vital sign before deciding what it means.","rationales":[{"en":"“Ignore the value because the client feels well” is not the best response. It dismisses clinically relevant information instead of assessing and documenting it. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: An unexpected reading should first be verified using correct technique. Dental hygienists assess and refer; they do not diagnose hypertension.","zh":"“Ignore the value because the client feels well”不是最佳处理。该做法忽略了具有临床意义的信息，而不是进行评估和记录。 正确处理原则是：异常读数应先用正确方法复测。牙科卫生师负责评估和转诊，而不是诊断高血压。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Begin instrumentation immediately” is not the best response. It moves ahead before the safety concern or current need has been assessed. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: An unexpected reading should first be verified using correct technique. Dental hygienists assess and refer; they do not diagnose hypertension.","zh":"“Begin instrumentation immediately”不是最佳处理。该做法在尚未评估安全问题或当前需要之前就继续治疗。 正确处理原则是：异常读数应先用正确方法复测。牙科卫生师负责评估和转诊，而不是诊断高血压。"},{"en":"“Diagnose hypertension” is not the best response. It exceeds the dental hygienist's role; the finding should be documented and appropriately referred. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: An unexpected reading should first be verified using correct technique. Dental hygienists assess and refer; they do not diagnose hypertension.","zh":"“Diagnose hypertension”不是最佳处理。这超出了牙科保健师的职责范围；应记录该发现并作适当转诊。 正确处理原则是：异常读数应先用正确方法复测。牙科卫生师负责评估和转诊，而不是诊断高血压。"}]},{"id":"poc-005","concept":"Extraoral/Intraoral Examination","stem":"During an intraoral examination, a white lesion does not wipe off and has persisted for three weeks. What is the BEST action?","choices":["Record it as normal variation","Re-evaluate in one year","Document the lesion fully and arrange timely referral or further evaluation","Remove it with an explorer"],"answer":2,"why":"A persistent non-wipeable lesion requires complete documentation and timely evaluation. Delayed follow-up could compromise care.","zh":"持续存在且不能擦除的白色病变需要完整记录并及时转诊或进一步评估。","pearl":"Persistent, unexplained oral lesions should not be casually watched for long intervals.","rationales":[{"en":"“Record it as normal variation” is not the best response. It dismisses clinically relevant information instead of assessing and documenting it. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: A persistent non-wipeable lesion requires complete documentation and timely evaluation. Delayed follow-up could compromise care.","zh":"“Record it as normal variation”不是最佳处理。该做法忽略了具有临床意义的信息，而不是进行评估和记录。 正确处理原则是：持续存在且不能擦除的白色病变需要完整记录并及时转诊或进一步评估。"},{"en":"“Re-evaluate in one year” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: A persistent non-wipeable lesion requires complete documentation and timely evaluation. Delayed follow-up could compromise care.","zh":"“Re-evaluate in one year”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：持续存在且不能擦除的白色病变需要完整记录并及时转诊或进一步评估。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Remove it with an explorer” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: A persistent non-wipeable lesion requires complete documentation and timely evaluation. Delayed follow-up could compromise care.","zh":"“Remove it with an explorer”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：持续存在且不能擦除的白色病变需要完整记录并及时转诊或进一步评估。"}]},{"id":"poc-006","concept":"Periodontal Assessment","stem":"Which finding is most useful for detecting current gingival inflammation?","choices":["Bleeding on probing","Existing restoration","Tooth colour","Previous extraction"],"answer":0,"why":"Bleeding on probing is a clinical sign of inflammatory response and contributes to periodontal assessment.","zh":"探诊出血是炎症反应的临床表现，是牙周评估的重要组成部分。","pearl":"Bone loss shows past destruction; bleeding helps identify current inflammation.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Existing restoration” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Bleeding on probing is a clinical sign of inflammatory response and contributes to periodontal assessment.","zh":"“Existing restoration”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：探诊出血是炎症反应的临床表现，是牙周评估的重要组成部分。"},{"en":"“Tooth colour” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Bleeding on probing is a clinical sign of inflammatory response and contributes to periodontal assessment.","zh":"“Tooth colour”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：探诊出血是炎症反应的临床表现，是牙周评估的重要组成部分。"},{"en":"“Previous extraction” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Bleeding on probing is a clinical sign of inflammatory response and contributes to periodontal assessment.","zh":"“Previous extraction”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：探诊出血是炎症反应的临床表现，是牙周评估的重要组成部分。"}]},{"id":"poc-007","concept":"Periodontal Assessment","stem":"A 6-mm probing depth is recorded around a tooth. Which additional finding is essential for interpreting attachment loss?","choices":["Client's age only","Gingival margin position relative to the CEJ","Tooth shade","Salivary pH only"],"answer":1,"why":"Clinical attachment level depends on probing depth and the location of the gingival margin relative to the CEJ.","zh":"临床附着水平取决于探诊深度以及龈缘相对于釉牙骨质界的位置。","pearl":"Pocket depth alone does not equal attachment loss.","rationales":[{"en":"“Client's age only” is not the best response. It is too narrow and omits other information required for safe, client-centred care. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Clinical attachment level depends on probing depth and the location of the gingival margin relative to the CEJ.","zh":"“Client's age only”不是最佳处理。该做法过于片面，遗漏了安全且以患者为中心的护理所需信息。 正确处理原则是：临床附着水平取决于探诊深度以及龈缘相对于釉牙骨质界的位置。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Tooth shade” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Clinical attachment level depends on probing depth and the location of the gingival margin relative to the CEJ.","zh":"“Tooth shade”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：临床附着水平取决于探诊深度以及龈缘相对于釉牙骨质界的位置。"},{"en":"“Salivary pH only” is not the best response. It is too narrow and omits other information required for safe, client-centred care. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Clinical attachment level depends on probing depth and the location of the gingival margin relative to the CEJ.","zh":"“Salivary pH only”不是最佳处理。该做法过于片面，遗漏了安全且以患者为中心的护理所需信息。 正确处理原则是：临床附着水平取决于探诊深度以及龈缘相对于釉牙骨质界的位置。"}]},{"id":"poc-008","concept":"Risk Assessment","stem":"A client has well-controlled diabetes, smokes daily, and has generalized bleeding on probing. Which factor most strongly increases periodontal risk?","choices":["Daily smoking","Controlled diabetes alone","Client's eye colour","Use of an electric toothbrush"],"answer":0,"why":"Smoking is a major modifiable periodontal risk factor and can significantly alter disease progression and treatment response.","zh":"吸烟是重要且可改变的牙周危险因素，会显著影响疾病进展和治疗反应。","pearl":"Risk assessment considers both disease indicators and modifiers.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Controlled diabetes alone” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Smoking is a major modifiable periodontal risk factor and can significantly alter disease progression and treatment response.","zh":"“Controlled diabetes alone”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：吸烟是重要且可改变的牙周危险因素，会显著影响疾病进展和治疗反应。"},{"en":"“Client's eye colour” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Smoking is a major modifiable periodontal risk factor and can significantly alter disease progression and treatment response.","zh":"“Client's eye colour”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：吸烟是重要且可改变的牙周危险因素，会显著影响疾病进展和治疗反应。"},{"en":"“Use of an electric toothbrush” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Smoking is a major modifiable periodontal risk factor and can significantly alter disease progression and treatment response.","zh":"“Use of an electric toothbrush”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：吸烟是重要且可改变的牙周危险因素，会显著影响疾病进展和治疗反应。"}]},{"id":"poc-009","concept":"Dental Hygiene Diagnosis","stem":"Which statement is written most like a dental hygiene diagnosis?","choices":["Chronic periodontitis","Ineffective plaque control related to limited interdental cleaning, evidenced by generalized interproximal biofilm and bleeding","Prescribe antibiotics","The client needs a filling"],"answer":1,"why":"A dental hygiene diagnosis identifies a client response or need that can be addressed within dental hygiene care and links it to supporting evidence.","zh":"牙科卫生诊断描述可由牙科卫生护理处理的患者需求，并以评估证据支持。","pearl":"Diagnosis connects the problem, contributing factors, and evidence.","rationales":[{"en":"“Chronic periodontitis” is not the best response. It represents a dental/medical diagnosis or treatment conclusion rather than a dental hygiene need statement. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: A dental hygiene diagnosis identifies a client response or need that can be addressed within dental hygiene care and links it to supporting evidence.","zh":"“Chronic periodontitis”不是最佳处理。这属于牙科或医学诊断/治疗结论，而不是牙科保健需要陈述。 正确处理原则是：牙科卫生诊断描述可由牙科卫生护理处理的患者需求，并以评估证据支持。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Prescribe antibiotics” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: A dental hygiene diagnosis identifies a client response or need that can be addressed within dental hygiene care and links it to supporting evidence.","zh":"“Prescribe antibiotics”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：牙科卫生诊断描述可由牙科卫生护理处理的患者需求，并以评估证据支持。"},{"en":"“The client needs a filling” is not the best response. It represents a dental/medical diagnosis or treatment conclusion rather than a dental hygiene need statement. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: A dental hygiene diagnosis identifies a client response or need that can be addressed within dental hygiene care and links it to supporting evidence.","zh":"“The client needs a filling”不是最佳处理。这属于牙科或医学诊断/治疗结论，而不是牙科保健需要陈述。 正确处理原则是：牙科卫生诊断描述可由牙科卫生护理处理的患者需求，并以评估证据支持。"}]},{"id":"poc-010","concept":"Dental Hygiene Diagnosis","stem":"What is the primary purpose of the dental hygiene diagnosis?","choices":["To replace the dentist's diagnosis","To identify client needs that guide dental hygiene interventions","To create a billing code only","To list every medical condition"],"answer":1,"why":"The dental hygiene diagnosis organizes assessment data into client needs that direct planning and care.","zh":"牙科卫生诊断将评估资料整理为患者需求，用于指导护理计划和干预。","pearl":"Assessment gathers data; diagnosis gives the data clinical meaning.","rationales":[{"en":"“To replace the dentist's diagnosis” is not the best response. It represents a dental/medical diagnosis or treatment conclusion rather than a dental hygiene need statement. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The dental hygiene diagnosis organizes assessment data into client needs that direct planning and care.","zh":"“To replace the dentist's diagnosis”不是最佳处理。这属于牙科或医学诊断/治疗结论，而不是牙科保健需要陈述。 正确处理原则是：牙科卫生诊断将评估资料整理为患者需求，用于指导护理计划和干预。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“To create a billing code only” is not the best response. It is too narrow and omits other information required for safe, client-centred care. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The dental hygiene diagnosis organizes assessment data into client needs that direct planning and care.","zh":"“To create a billing code only”不是最佳处理。该做法过于片面，遗漏了安全且以患者为中心的护理所需信息。 正确处理原则是：牙科卫生诊断将评估资料整理为患者需求，用于指导护理计划和干预。"},{"en":"“To list every medical condition” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The dental hygiene diagnosis organizes assessment data into client needs that direct planning and care.","zh":"“To list every medical condition”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：牙科卫生诊断将评估资料整理为患者需求，用于指导护理计划和干预。"}]},{"id":"poc-011","concept":"Planning","stem":"Which goal is most client-centred and measurable?","choices":["Client will improve oral hygiene","Client will reduce bleeding sites from 60% to 25% within eight weeks","Hygienist will explain flossing","Client should try harder"],"answer":1,"why":"A strong goal is specific, measurable, realistic, relevant, and time-bound.","zh":"优质目标应具体、可测量、现实、相关且有时间限制。","pearl":"A measurable goal states what will change, by how much, and by when.","rationales":[{"en":"“Client will improve oral hygiene” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: A strong goal is specific, measurable, realistic, relevant, and time-bound.","zh":"“Client will improve oral hygiene”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：优质目标应具体、可测量、现实、相关且有时间限制。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Hygienist will explain flossing” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: A strong goal is specific, measurable, realistic, relevant, and time-bound.","zh":"“Hygienist will explain flossing”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：优质目标应具体、可测量、现实、相关且有时间限制。"},{"en":"“Client should try harder” is not the best response. It labels or pressures the client instead of identifying barriers and supporting achievable change. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: A strong goal is specific, measurable, realistic, relevant, and time-bound.","zh":"“Client should try harder”不是最佳处理。该做法给患者贴标签或施压，而不是识别障碍并支持可实现的改变。 正确处理原则是：优质目标应具体、可测量、现实、相关且有时间限制。"}]},{"id":"poc-012","concept":"Planning","stem":"A client has acute oral pain, heavy calculus, and limited knowledge of home care. Which concern should generally be addressed first?","choices":["Long-term esthetic polishing","The acute problem affecting comfort and safety","A six-month recare date","Whitening options"],"answer":1,"why":"Care planning prioritizes urgent and safety-related needs before elective or long-term goals.","zh":"护理计划应先处理影响舒适和安全的紧急问题，再处理选择性或长期目标。","pearl":"Prioritize urgent, unstable, and safety-related needs first.","rationales":[{"en":"“Long-term esthetic polishing” is not the best response. It is a lower-priority elective issue and does not address the immediate clinical concern. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Care planning prioritizes urgent and safety-related needs before elective or long-term goals.","zh":"“Long-term esthetic polishing”不是最佳处理。这是优先级较低的选择性事项，不能处理当前紧迫的临床问题。 正确处理原则是：护理计划应先处理影响舒适和安全的紧急问题，再处理选择性或长期目标。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“A six-month recare date” is not the best response. It is a lower-priority elective issue and does not address the immediate clinical concern. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Care planning prioritizes urgent and safety-related needs before elective or long-term goals.","zh":"“A six-month recare date”不是最佳处理。这是优先级较低的选择性事项，不能处理当前紧迫的临床问题。 正确处理原则是：护理计划应先处理影响舒适和安全的紧急问题，再处理选择性或长期目标。"},{"en":"“Whitening options” is not the best response. It is a lower-priority elective issue and does not address the immediate clinical concern. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Care planning prioritizes urgent and safety-related needs before elective or long-term goals.","zh":"“Whitening options”不是最佳处理。这是优先级较低的选择性事项，不能处理当前紧迫的临床问题。 正确处理原则是：护理计划应先处理影响舒适和安全的紧急问题，再处理选择性或长期目标。"}]},{"id":"poc-013","concept":"Planning","stem":"What should happen before a care plan is finalized?","choices":["The client should participate in reviewing options and goals","The hygienist should choose without discussion","All treatment must be completed","The record should be closed"],"answer":0,"why":"Collaborative planning supports informed consent, autonomy, and realistic goals.","zh":"共同制定计划有助于知情同意、尊重自主权并建立现实目标。","pearl":"A technically perfect plan can still fail if the client did not help shape it.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“The hygienist should choose without discussion” is not the best response. It excludes the client from decisions and is inconsistent with informed, shared decision-making. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Collaborative planning supports informed consent, autonomy, and realistic goals.","zh":"“The hygienist should choose without discussion”不是最佳处理。该做法排除了患者参与，不符合知情和共同决策原则。 正确处理原则是：共同制定计划有助于知情同意、尊重自主权并建立现实目标。"},{"en":"“All treatment must be completed” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Collaborative planning supports informed consent, autonomy, and realistic goals.","zh":"“All treatment must be completed”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：共同制定计划有助于知情同意、尊重自主权并建立现实目标。"},{"en":"“The record should be closed” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Collaborative planning supports informed consent, autonomy, and realistic goals.","zh":"“The record should be closed”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：共同制定计划有助于知情同意、尊重自主权并建立现实目标。"}]},{"id":"poc-014","concept":"Informed Consent","stem":"Valid informed consent requires the client to understand:","choices":["Only the cost","The proposed care, material risks, benefits, alternatives, and consequences of declining","Only the clinician's preferred option","Every rare event ever reported"],"answer":1,"why":"Consent requires meaningful information, capacity, voluntariness, and an opportunity to ask questions.","zh":"有效知情同意需要提供治疗内容、主要风险、益处、替代方案及拒绝治疗的后果，并确保患者有能力且自愿决定。","pearl":"A signature is evidence of consent, not the whole consent process.","rationales":[{"en":"“Only the cost” is not the best response. It is too narrow and omits other information required for safe, client-centred care. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Consent requires meaningful information, capacity, voluntariness, and an opportunity to ask questions.","zh":"“Only the cost”不是最佳处理。该做法过于片面，遗漏了安全且以患者为中心的护理所需信息。 正确处理原则是：有效知情同意需要提供治疗内容、主要风险、益处、替代方案及拒绝治疗的后果，并确保患者有能力且自愿决定。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Only the clinician's preferred option” is not the best response. It is too narrow and omits other information required for safe, client-centred care. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Consent requires meaningful information, capacity, voluntariness, and an opportunity to ask questions.","zh":"“Only the clinician's preferred option”不是最佳处理。该做法过于片面，遗漏了安全且以患者为中心的护理所需信息。 正确处理原则是：有效知情同意需要提供治疗内容、主要风险、益处、替代方案及拒绝治疗的后果，并确保患者有能力且自愿决定。"},{"en":"“Every rare event ever reported” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Consent requires meaningful information, capacity, voluntariness, and an opportunity to ask questions.","zh":"“Every rare event ever reported”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：有效知情同意需要提供治疗内容、主要风险、益处、替代方案及拒绝治疗的后果，并确保患者有能力且自愿决定。"}]},{"id":"poc-015","concept":"Informed Consent","stem":"A capable client refuses recommended radiographs after the risks and alternatives are explained. What should the hygienist do?","choices":["Take them anyway","Respect the refusal, document the discussion, and determine whether safe care can still be provided","Dismiss the client immediately","Ask a family member to override the decision"],"answer":1,"why":"Capable clients may refuse care. The clinician must document informed refusal and decide whether remaining care can be delivered safely and ethically.","zh":"有决定能力的患者可以拒绝治疗。应记录知情拒绝，并判断是否仍能安全、合乎伦理地提供其他护理。","pearl":"Autonomy permits refusal; professional responsibility still limits unsafe care.","rationales":[{"en":"“Take them anyway” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Capable clients may refuse care. The clinician must document informed refusal and decide whether remaining care can be delivered safely and ethically.","zh":"“Take them anyway”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：有决定能力的患者可以拒绝治疗。应记录知情拒绝，并判断是否仍能安全、合乎伦理地提供其他护理。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Dismiss the client immediately” is not the best response. It is punitive rather than respectful, therapeutic, and clinically justified. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Capable clients may refuse care. The clinician must document informed refusal and decide whether remaining care can be delivered safely and ethically.","zh":"“Dismiss the client immediately”不是最佳处理。该做法带有惩罚性，而非尊重、治疗性和有临床依据。 正确处理原则是：有决定能力的患者可以拒绝治疗。应记录知情拒绝，并判断是否仍能安全、合乎伦理地提供其他护理。"},{"en":"“Ask a family member to override the decision” is not the best response. A capable client's decision cannot be overridden by another person. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Capable clients may refuse care. The clinician must document informed refusal and decide whether remaining care can be delivered safely and ethically.","zh":"“Ask a family member to override the decision”不是最佳处理。有决策能力患者的决定不能由他人推翻。 正确处理原则是：有决定能力的患者可以拒绝治疗。应记录知情拒绝，并判断是否仍能安全、合乎伦理地提供其他护理。"}]},{"id":"poc-016","concept":"Implementation","stem":"During instrumentation, the client develops wheezing and difficulty speaking. What should the hygienist do first?","choices":["Continue quickly","Stop treatment and begin emergency assessment and management","Finish polishing","Document it at the end"],"answer":1,"why":"A change in the client's condition requires immediate reassessment and appropriate emergency response.","zh":"患者状况发生变化时，应立即停止治疗、重新评估并进行适当急救处理。","pearl":"Implementation is never automatic; reassessment continues throughout care.","rationales":[{"en":"“Continue quickly” is not the best response. It moves ahead before the safety concern or current need has been assessed. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: A change in the client's condition requires immediate reassessment and appropriate emergency response.","zh":"“Continue quickly”不是最佳处理。该做法在尚未评估安全问题或当前需要之前就继续治疗。 正确处理原则是：患者状况发生变化时，应立即停止治疗、重新评估并进行适当急救处理。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Finish polishing” is not the best response. It moves ahead before the safety concern or current need has been assessed. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: A change in the client's condition requires immediate reassessment and appropriate emergency response.","zh":"“Finish polishing”不是最佳处理。该做法在尚未评估安全问题或当前需要之前就继续治疗。 正确处理原则是：患者状况发生变化时，应立即停止治疗、重新评估并进行适当急救处理。"},{"en":"“Document it at the end” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: A change in the client's condition requires immediate reassessment and appropriate emergency response.","zh":"“Document it at the end”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：患者状况发生变化时，应立即停止治疗、重新评估并进行适当急救处理。"}]},{"id":"poc-017","concept":"Implementation","stem":"Which teaching strategy best supports client-centred implementation?","choices":["Give the same instructions to every client","Use plain language, demonstrate the skill, and ask the client to show it back","Provide a long lecture only","Avoid checking understanding"],"answer":1,"why":"Tailored instruction and teach-back confirm understanding and skill, making behaviour change more achievable.","zh":"使用简明语言、示范并让患者回示，可以确认理解和技能，更有利于行为改变。","pearl":"Teach-back tests the clarity of the teaching, not the intelligence of the client.","rationales":[{"en":"“Give the same instructions to every client” is not the best response. It does not adapt communication or verify the client's understanding and ability. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Tailored instruction and teach-back confirm understanding and skill, making behaviour change more achievable.","zh":"“Give the same instructions to every client”不是最佳处理。该做法未调整沟通方式，也未确认患者的理解和操作能力。 正确处理原则是：使用简明语言、示范并让患者回示，可以确认理解和技能，更有利于行为改变。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Provide a long lecture only” is not the best response. It is too narrow and omits other information required for safe, client-centred care. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Tailored instruction and teach-back confirm understanding and skill, making behaviour change more achievable.","zh":"“Provide a long lecture only”不是最佳处理。该做法过于片面，遗漏了安全且以患者为中心的护理所需信息。 正确处理原则是：使用简明语言、示范并让患者回示，可以确认理解和技能，更有利于行为改变。"},{"en":"“Avoid checking understanding” is not the best response. It does not adapt communication or verify the client's understanding and ability. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Tailored instruction and teach-back confirm understanding and skill, making behaviour change more achievable.","zh":"“Avoid checking understanding”不是最佳处理。该做法未调整沟通方式，也未确认患者的理解和操作能力。 正确处理原则是：使用简明语言、示范并让患者回示，可以确认理解和技能，更有利于行为改变。"}]},{"id":"poc-018","concept":"Implementation","stem":"A planned intervention becomes contraindicated because the client's health status changes. What is the BEST response?","choices":["Follow the original plan exactly","Modify or postpone care and document the reason","Delete the original assessment","Ask the client to decide whether it is safe"],"answer":1,"why":"The care plan must remain responsive to current assessment findings and safety considerations.","zh":"护理计划必须根据最新评估结果和安全因素进行调整或延期，并记录原因。","pearl":"The care plan is a living clinical document, not a train locked to one track.","rationales":[{"en":"“Follow the original plan exactly” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The care plan must remain responsive to current assessment findings and safety considerations.","zh":"“Follow the original plan exactly”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：护理计划必须根据最新评估结果和安全因素进行调整或延期，并记录原因。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Delete the original assessment” is not the best response. It compromises record integrity by obscuring or changing the original clinical information. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The care plan must remain responsive to current assessment findings and safety considerations.","zh":"“Delete the original assessment”不是最佳处理。该做法会遮盖或更改原始临床信息，损害病历完整性。 正确处理原则是：护理计划必须根据最新评估结果和安全因素进行调整或延期，并记录原因。"},{"en":"“Ask the client to decide whether it is safe” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The care plan must remain responsive to current assessment findings and safety considerations.","zh":"“Ask the client to decide whether it is safe”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：护理计划必须根据最新评估结果和安全因素进行调整或延期，并记录原因。"}]},{"id":"poc-019","concept":"Evaluation","stem":"At re-evaluation, bleeding on probing decreases from 70% to 30%, but the goal was below 20%. How should this be interpreted?","choices":["No improvement occurred","The goal was fully met","Meaningful improvement occurred, but the goal was only partially met","The original data should be discarded"],"answer":2,"why":"Evaluation compares outcomes with baseline and the stated goal. The client improved, but the planned target was not reached.","zh":"评价应将结果与基线和既定目标比较。患者已有改善，但尚未达到目标。","pearl":"Evaluation is not merely pass or fail; partial progress guides the next plan.","rationales":[{"en":"“No improvement occurred” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Evaluation compares outcomes with baseline and the stated goal. The client improved, but the planned target was not reached.","zh":"“No improvement occurred”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：评价应将结果与基线和既定目标比较。患者已有改善，但尚未达到目标。"},{"en":"“The goal was fully met” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Evaluation compares outcomes with baseline and the stated goal. The client improved, but the planned target was not reached.","zh":"“The goal was fully met”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：评价应将结果与基线和既定目标比较。患者已有改善，但尚未达到目标。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“The original data should be discarded” is not the best response. It compromises record integrity by obscuring or changing the original clinical information. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Evaluation compares outcomes with baseline and the stated goal. The client improved, but the planned target was not reached.","zh":"“The original data should be discarded”不是最佳处理。该做法会遮盖或更改原始临床信息，损害病历完整性。 正确处理原则是：评价应将结果与基线和既定目标比较。患者已有改善，但尚未达到目标。"}]},{"id":"poc-020","concept":"Evaluation","stem":"Which action best represents evaluation?","choices":["Collecting the original medical history","Comparing post-care outcomes with baseline findings and goals","Selecting instruments","Obtaining initial consent"],"answer":1,"why":"Evaluation determines whether interventions achieved the intended outcomes and whether the plan should continue or change.","zh":"评价是将治疗后结果与基线和目标比较，以判断干预是否有效以及是否需要调整计划。","pearl":"Without a baseline and measurable goal, evaluation becomes guesswork.","rationales":[{"en":"“Collecting the original medical history” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Evaluation determines whether interventions achieved the intended outcomes and whether the plan should continue or change.","zh":"“Collecting the original medical history”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：评价是将治疗后结果与基线和目标比较，以判断干预是否有效以及是否需要调整计划。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Selecting instruments” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Evaluation determines whether interventions achieved the intended outcomes and whether the plan should continue or change.","zh":"“Selecting instruments”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：评价是将治疗后结果与基线和目标比较，以判断干预是否有效以及是否需要调整计划。"},{"en":"“Obtaining initial consent” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Evaluation determines whether interventions achieved the intended outcomes and whether the plan should continue or change.","zh":"“Obtaining initial consent”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：评价是将治疗后结果与基线和目标比较，以判断干预是否有效以及是否需要调整计划。"}]},{"id":"poc-021","concept":"Documentation","stem":"Which entry is the most appropriate clinical documentation?","choices":["Client was difficult","Generalized bleeding noted; OHI reviewed with interdental brush demonstration; client successfully demonstrated technique","Everything normal","Good appointment"],"answer":1,"why":"Clinical records should be objective, specific, relevant, and describe findings, care, client response, and follow-up.","zh":"临床记录应客观、具体、相关，并说明发现、提供的护理、患者反应及后续安排。","pearl":"Document observable facts and professional actions, not labels or judgments.","rationales":[{"en":"“Client was difficult” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Clinical records should be objective, specific, relevant, and describe findings, care, client response, and follow-up.","zh":"“Client was difficult”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：临床记录应客观、具体、相关，并说明发现、提供的护理、患者反应及后续安排。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Everything normal” is not the best response. It dismisses clinically relevant information instead of assessing and documenting it. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Clinical records should be objective, specific, relevant, and describe findings, care, client response, and follow-up.","zh":"“Everything normal”不是最佳处理。该做法忽略了具有临床意义的信息，而不是进行评估和记录。 正确处理原则是：临床记录应客观、具体、相关，并说明发现、提供的护理、患者反应及后续安排。"},{"en":"“Good appointment” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Clinical records should be objective, specific, relevant, and describe findings, care, client response, and follow-up.","zh":"“Good appointment”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：临床记录应客观、具体、相关，并说明发现、提供的护理、患者反应及后续安排。"}]},{"id":"poc-022","concept":"Documentation","stem":"An error is discovered in a completed clinical record. What is the BEST correction method?","choices":["Erase the original entry completely","Alter the date so the record looks correct","Make a transparent correction according to policy without obscuring the original entry","Delete the entire note"],"answer":2,"why":"Records must preserve integrity. Corrections should remain traceable and follow regulatory and workplace requirements.","zh":"病历必须保持完整性。更正应可追溯，不应掩盖原始记录，并遵循相关规定。","pearl":"A corrected record should show what changed, when, and by whom.","rationales":[{"en":"“Erase the original entry completely” is not the best response. It compromises record integrity by obscuring or changing the original clinical information. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Records must preserve integrity. Corrections should remain traceable and follow regulatory and workplace requirements.","zh":"“Erase the original entry completely”不是最佳处理。该做法会遮盖或更改原始临床信息，损害病历完整性。 正确处理原则是：病历必须保持完整性。更正应可追溯，不应掩盖原始记录，并遵循相关规定。"},{"en":"“Alter the date so the record looks correct” is not the best response. It compromises record integrity by obscuring or changing the original clinical information. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Records must preserve integrity. Corrections should remain traceable and follow regulatory and workplace requirements.","zh":"“Alter the date so the record looks correct”不是最佳处理。该做法会遮盖或更改原始临床信息，损害病历完整性。 正确处理原则是：病历必须保持完整性。更正应可追溯，不应掩盖原始记录，并遵循相关规定。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Delete the entire note” is not the best response. It compromises record integrity by obscuring or changing the original clinical information. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Records must preserve integrity. Corrections should remain traceable and follow regulatory and workplace requirements.","zh":"“Delete the entire note”不是最佳处理。该做法会遮盖或更改原始临床信息，损害病历完整性。 正确处理原则是：病历必须保持完整性。更正应可追溯，不应掩盖原始记录，并遵循相关规定。"}]},{"id":"poc-023","concept":"Documentation","stem":"Why should a client's refusal of recommended care be documented?","choices":["To punish the client","To record the information provided, the client's decision, and the plan for safe follow-up","Because refusal removes all clinician responsibility","Only for billing"],"answer":1,"why":"Documentation of informed refusal supports continuity, communication, and accountability.","zh":"记录知情拒绝有助于持续护理、沟通和专业责任。","pearl":"Record the discussion and decision, not merely the word “refused.”","rationales":[{"en":"“To punish the client” is not the best response. It is punitive rather than respectful, therapeutic, and clinically justified. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Documentation of informed refusal supports continuity, communication, and accountability.","zh":"“To punish the client”不是最佳处理。该做法带有惩罚性，而非尊重、治疗性和有临床依据。 正确处理原则是：记录知情拒绝有助于持续护理、沟通和专业责任。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Because refusal removes all clinician responsibility” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Documentation of informed refusal supports continuity, communication, and accountability.","zh":"“Because refusal removes all clinician responsibility”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：记录知情拒绝有助于持续护理、沟通和专业责任。"},{"en":"“Only for billing” is not the best response. It is too narrow and omits other information required for safe, client-centred care. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Documentation of informed refusal supports continuity, communication, and accountability.","zh":"“Only for billing”不是最佳处理。该做法过于片面，遗漏了安全且以患者为中心的护理所需信息。 正确处理原则是：记录知情拒绝有助于持续护理、沟通和专业责任。"}]},{"id":"poc-024","concept":"Sequencing","stem":"Which sequence best represents the dental hygiene process of care?","choices":["Implementation, assessment, evaluation, diagnosis, planning","Assessment, dental hygiene diagnosis, planning, implementation, evaluation","Planning, evaluation, assessment, implementation, diagnosis","Diagnosis, implementation, assessment, evaluation, planning"],"answer":1,"why":"The core sequence moves from assessment to diagnosis, planning, implementation, and evaluation, with documentation throughout.","zh":"牙科卫生护理过程依次为评估、牙科卫生诊断、计划、实施和评价，记录贯穿全过程。","pearl":"Documentation runs through every phase rather than appearing only at the end.","rationales":[{"en":"“Implementation, assessment, evaluation, diagnosis, planning” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The core sequence moves from assessment to diagnosis, planning, implementation, and evaluation, with documentation throughout.","zh":"“Implementation, assessment, evaluation, diagnosis, planning”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：牙科卫生护理过程依次为评估、牙科卫生诊断、计划、实施和评价，记录贯穿全过程。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Planning, evaluation, assessment, implementation, diagnosis” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The core sequence moves from assessment to diagnosis, planning, implementation, and evaluation, with documentation throughout.","zh":"“Planning, evaluation, assessment, implementation, diagnosis”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：牙科卫生护理过程依次为评估、牙科卫生诊断、计划、实施和评价，记录贯穿全过程。"},{"en":"“Diagnosis, implementation, assessment, evaluation, planning” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The core sequence moves from assessment to diagnosis, planning, implementation, and evaluation, with documentation throughout.","zh":"“Diagnosis, implementation, assessment, evaluation, planning”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：牙科卫生护理过程依次为评估、牙科卫生诊断、计划、实施和评价，记录贯穿全过程。"}]},{"id":"poc-025","concept":"Sequencing","stem":"A client returns after periodontal debridement. Before repeating the same intervention, the hygienist should first:","choices":["Reassess outcomes and current needs","Assume the original findings remain unchanged","Repeat treatment automatically","Schedule whitening"],"answer":0,"why":"Reassessment and evaluation determine whether the intervention worked and what the client needs next.","zh":"再次干预前应重新评估结果和当前需求，以确定原治疗是否有效以及下一步措施。","pearl":"The next cycle begins with new assessment, not autopilot.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Assume the original findings remain unchanged” is not the best response. It relies on an unverified assumption instead of current assessment data. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Reassessment and evaluation determine whether the intervention worked and what the client needs next.","zh":"“Assume the original findings remain unchanged”不是最佳处理。该做法依赖未经核实的假设，而不是当前评估数据。 正确处理原则是：再次干预前应重新评估结果和当前需求，以确定原治疗是否有效以及下一步措施。"},{"en":"“Repeat treatment automatically” is not the best response. It moves ahead before the safety concern or current need has been assessed. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Reassessment and evaluation determine whether the intervention worked and what the client needs next.","zh":"“Repeat treatment automatically”不是最佳处理。该做法在尚未评估安全问题或当前需要之前就继续治疗。 正确处理原则是：再次干预前应重新评估结果和当前需求，以确定原治疗是否有效以及下一步措施。"},{"en":"“Schedule whitening” is not the best response. It is a lower-priority elective issue and does not address the immediate clinical concern. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Reassessment and evaluation determine whether the intervention worked and what the client needs next.","zh":"“Schedule whitening”不是最佳处理。这是优先级较低的选择性事项，不能处理当前紧迫的临床问题。 正确处理原则是：再次干预前应重新评估结果和当前需求，以确定原治疗是否有效以及下一步措施。"}]},{"id":"poc-026","concept":"Client-Centred Care","stem":"A client identifies reducing sensitivity as their main concern, while the hygienist is focused on plaque scores. What is the BEST approach?","choices":["Ignore the client's concern","Integrate the client's priority into assessment and planning while addressing clinical needs","Promise sensitivity will disappear","Treat only what the clinician prefers"],"answer":1,"why":"Client-centred care balances professional findings with the client's values, concerns, and readiness.","zh":"以患者为中心的护理应在满足临床需要的同时，纳入患者的价值观、主要关注点和准备程度。","pearl":"The client's chief concern is clinically useful data, not a side note.","rationales":[{"en":"“Ignore the client's concern” is not the best response. It dismisses clinically relevant information instead of assessing and documenting it. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Client-centred care balances professional findings with the client's values, concerns, and readiness.","zh":"“Ignore the client's concern”不是最佳处理。该做法忽略了具有临床意义的信息，而不是进行评估和记录。 正确处理原则是：以患者为中心的护理应在满足临床需要的同时，纳入患者的价值观、主要关注点和准备程度。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Promise sensitivity will disappear” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Client-centred care balances professional findings with the client's values, concerns, and readiness.","zh":"“Promise sensitivity will disappear”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：以患者为中心的护理应在满足临床需要的同时，纳入患者的价值观、主要关注点和准备程度。"},{"en":"“Treat only what the clinician prefers” is not the best response. It is too narrow and omits other information required for safe, client-centred care. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Client-centred care balances professional findings with the client's values, concerns, and readiness.","zh":"“Treat only what the clinician prefers”不是最佳处理。该做法过于片面，遗漏了安全且以患者为中心的护理所需信息。 正确处理原则是：以患者为中心的护理应在满足临床需要的同时，纳入患者的价值观、主要关注点和准备程度。"}]},{"id":"poc-027","concept":"Client-Centred Care","stem":"Which action best supports shared decision-making?","choices":["Present one option as the only acceptable choice","Discuss reasonable options and invite the client to weigh them according to personal values","Use technical language to discourage questions","Ask for a signature before explaining care"],"answer":1,"why":"Shared decision-making combines professional evidence with informed client preferences.","zh":"共同决策将专业证据与患者在充分知情后的偏好结合起来。","pearl":"Shared decisions require real options and a real voice.","rationales":[{"en":"“Present one option as the only acceptable choice” is not the best response. It is too narrow and omits other information required for safe, client-centred care. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Shared decision-making combines professional evidence with informed client preferences.","zh":"“Present one option as the only acceptable choice”不是最佳处理。该做法过于片面，遗漏了安全且以患者为中心的护理所需信息。 正确处理原则是：共同决策将专业证据与患者在充分知情后的偏好结合起来。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Use technical language to discourage questions” is not the best response. It does not adapt communication or verify the client's understanding and ability. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Shared decision-making combines professional evidence with informed client preferences.","zh":"“Use technical language to discourage questions”不是最佳处理。该做法未调整沟通方式，也未确认患者的理解和操作能力。 正确处理原则是：共同决策将专业证据与患者在充分知情后的偏好结合起来。"},{"en":"“Ask for a signature before explaining care” is not the best response. A signature cannot replace assessment, disclosure, understanding, or valid consent. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Shared decision-making combines professional evidence with informed client preferences.","zh":"“Ask for a signature before explaining care”不是最佳处理。签字不能取代评估、信息披露、理解和有效同意。 正确处理原则是：共同决策将专业证据与患者在充分知情后的偏好结合起来。"}]},{"id":"poc-028","concept":"Referral and Collaboration","stem":"An assessment finding is outside the dental hygienist's scope to diagnose. What is the BEST action?","choices":["Ignore it","Provide a definitive diagnosis anyway","Document the finding and make an appropriate referral or consultation","Ask the client to search online"],"answer":2,"why":"The hygienist should recognize findings, communicate them, and collaborate or refer when diagnosis or management is beyond scope.","zh":"当诊断或处理超出执业范围时，应识别并记录发现，进行适当转诊或会诊。","pearl":"Recognizing a problem is not the same as claiming authority to diagnose it.","rationales":[{"en":"“Ignore it” is not the best response. It dismisses clinically relevant information instead of assessing and documenting it. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The hygienist should recognize findings, communicate them, and collaborate or refer when diagnosis or management is beyond scope.","zh":"“Ignore it”不是最佳处理。该做法忽略了具有临床意义的信息，而不是进行评估和记录。 正确处理原则是：当诊断或处理超出执业范围时，应识别并记录发现，进行适当转诊或会诊。"},{"en":"“Provide a definitive diagnosis anyway” is not the best response. It exceeds the dental hygienist's role; the finding should be documented and appropriately referred. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The hygienist should recognize findings, communicate them, and collaborate or refer when diagnosis or management is beyond scope.","zh":"“Provide a definitive diagnosis anyway”不是最佳处理。这超出了牙科保健师的职责范围；应记录该发现并作适当转诊。 正确处理原则是：当诊断或处理超出执业范围时，应识别并记录发现，进行适当转诊或会诊。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Ask the client to search online” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The hygienist should recognize findings, communicate them, and collaborate or refer when diagnosis or management is beyond scope.","zh":"“Ask the client to search online”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：当诊断或处理超出执业范围时，应识别并记录发现，进行适当转诊或会诊。"}]},{"id":"poc-029","concept":"Quality Improvement","stem":"A clinic notices that many clients miss recommended re-evaluation appointments. Which response best reflects quality improvement?","choices":["Blame the clients","Review the process, identify barriers, test a reminder strategy, and measure whether attendance improves","Stop scheduling re-evaluations","Change the records"],"answer":1,"why":"Quality improvement uses data to identify a system problem, test a change, and evaluate outcomes.","zh":"质量改进利用数据识别系统问题、测试改进措施并评价结果。","pearl":"Quality improvement studies the process, not just the person.","rationales":[{"en":"“Blame the clients” is not the best response. It is punitive rather than respectful, therapeutic, and clinically justified. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Quality improvement uses data to identify a system problem, test a change, and evaluate outcomes.","zh":"“Blame the clients”不是最佳处理。该做法带有惩罚性，而非尊重、治疗性和有临床依据。 正确处理原则是：质量改进利用数据识别系统问题、测试改进措施并评价结果。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Stop scheduling re-evaluations” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Quality improvement uses data to identify a system problem, test a change, and evaluate outcomes.","zh":"“Stop scheduling re-evaluations”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：质量改进利用数据识别系统问题、测试改进措施并评价结果。"},{"en":"“Change the records” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: Quality improvement uses data to identify a system problem, test a change, and evaluate outcomes.","zh":"“Change the records”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：质量改进利用数据识别系统问题、测试改进措施并评价结果。"}]},{"id":"poc-030","concept":"Comprehensive Case","stem":"A client with generalized inflammation has not used interdental aids and says, “I do not think I can manage floss.” Which plan is BEST?","choices":["Document noncompliance and end the discussion","Select an easier interdental aid, demonstrate it, use teach-back, and set a measurable short-term goal","Insist on floss only","Delay all education until disease resolves"],"answer":1,"why":"The plan addresses the clinical need while respecting ability and readiness. A suitable aid, teach-back, and measurable goal support achievable change.","zh":"该计划在满足临床需要的同时考虑患者能力和准备程度。选择合适工具、回示教学和可测量目标更有利于行为改变。","pearl":"Adapt the method without abandoning the clinical objective.","rationales":[{"en":"“Document noncompliance and end the discussion” is not the best response. It labels or pressures the client instead of identifying barriers and supporting achievable change. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The plan addresses the clinical need while respecting ability and readiness. A suitable aid, teach-back, and measurable goal support achievable change.","zh":"“Document noncompliance and end the discussion”不是最佳处理。该做法给患者贴标签或施压，而不是识别障碍并支持可实现的改变。 正确处理原则是：该计划在满足临床需要的同时考虑患者能力和准备程度。选择合适工具、回示教学和可测量目标更有利于行为改变。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it directly follows the principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它直接符合上方解释的原则。"},{"en":"“Insist on floss only” is not the best response. It is too narrow and omits other information required for safe, client-centred care. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The plan addresses the clinical need while respecting ability and readiness. A suitable aid, teach-back, and measurable goal support achievable change.","zh":"“Insist on floss only”不是最佳处理。该做法过于片面，遗漏了安全且以患者为中心的护理所需信息。 正确处理原则是：该计划在满足临床需要的同时考虑患者能力和准备程度。选择合适工具、回示教学和可测量目标更有利于行为改变。"},{"en":"“Delay all education until disease resolves” is not the best response. It does not address the key assessment, safety, consent, or care-planning requirement in this situation. The required approach is reflected in the correct rationale: The plan addresses the clinical need while respecting ability and readiness. A suitable aid, teach-back, and measurable goal support achievable change.","zh":"“Delay all education until disease resolves”不是最佳处理。该选项未能处理此情境中的关键评估、安全、同意或护理计划要求。 正确处理原则是：该计划在满足临床需要的同时考虑患者能力和准备程度。选择合适工具、回示教学和可测量目标更有利于行为改变。"}]}];